.MCD 25000 0
.CMD SURFACEFORMAT rot=10 tilt=35 vScale=20 size=15,30
.CMD SKETCHFORMAT mag=1.000000,1.000000 center=0.500000,0.500000 size=15,30 box=y
.CMD PLOTFORMAT logs=0,0 subdivs=1,1 size=5,15 type=l
.CMD FORMAT  rd=d ct=10 im=i et=3 zt=15 pr=3 mass length time charge
.CMD SET ORIGIN 0
.CMD SET TOL 0.001000000000000
.CMD MARGIN 0
.CMD LINELENGTH 78
.CMD SET PRNCOLWIDTH 8
.CMD SET PRNPRECISION 4
.TXT 0 0 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,91
420scd.mcd to show the effects of cibic phase error in the channel's  
frequency response.
.TXT 3 0 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,82
1. Define the degraded phase of the channel's frequency response- in 'DFT 
form'.
.EQN 3 0 1 10 
N:128
.EQN 0 11 1 16 
n:0;N-1
.EQN 0 17 1 12 
j:0;2
.EQN 0 14 2 16 
î[j:-0.005*j
.EQN 0 18 3 15 
é[(n,j):î[j*n^3
.EQN 4 -59 2 62 
H[(n,j):if(nó8,exp(1i*é[(n,j)),if(nò120,exp(-1i*é[(N-n,j)),0))
.EQN 4 7 8 53 
0&-ã&é[(n,0),é[(n,1),é[(n,2){1,1,7,30,l}@8&0&n
.TXT 9 -8 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,135
2. Define the pulse whose spectrum has been shaped for low sidelobes: We 
choose a simple model, the triangle spectrum- in 'DFT form'.
.EQN 3 0 2 45 
P[n:if(nó8,8-n,if(nò120,n-120,0))
.EQN 0 50 7 20 
&&P[n{1,1,6,15,l}@N-1&0&n
.TXT 8 -50 1 32003 
b1,32002,78,35
3. Compute the output pulse, s(t).
.EQN 2 0 4 25 
idft(v):(1/\N)*cfft(v)
.EQN 0 29 2 17 
S[(n,j):H[(n,j)*P[n
.EQN 0 23 2 20 
s{52}j:idft(S{52}j)
.EQN 3 -26 3 17 
M[j:max(s{52}j)
.EQN 0 18 5 35 
s[(n,j):20*log(|s[(n,j)/M[j+0.000001)
.EQN 6 -27 9 58 
0&-40&s[(n,0),s[(n,1),s[(n,2){4,8,8,35,l}@N-1&0&n
.EQN 1 -17 5 9 
é[(8,j)=
.TXT 9 0 4 32003 
b4,32002,78,280
Note that a small cubic phase error also has a vary degrading effect upon the 
system response!! As a cubic has a nonzero best linear fit, there is a delay 
associated with this type of phase error. Note the asymmetry of the response: 
the first sidelobe comes up very rapidly !!
